    <item>
      <title>First Model</title>
      <link>https://choco-solver.org/tutos/first-example/first-model/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jan 2020 11:47:58 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>https://choco-solver.org/tutos/first-example/first-model/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;First of all, let&amp;rsquo;s consider the eight queen puzzle, frequently used to&#xA;introduce constraint programming.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_queens_puzzle&#34;&gt;Wikipedia&lt;/a&gt; told us&#xA;that:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The eight queens puzzle is the problem of placing eight chess queens&#xA;on an 8x8 chessboard so that no two queens threaten each other. Thus,&#xA;a solution requires that no two queens share the same row, column, or&#xA;diagonal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem can be generalized to the &lt;em&gt;n&lt;/em&gt;-queens problem (placing &lt;em&gt;n&lt;/em&gt;&#xA;queens on a nxn chessboard).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Follow-Up</title>
      <link>https://choco-solver.org/tutos/first-example/follow-up/</link>
